    "text": "Almost. It is on Thursday at two, and the hall is booked. I want visitors to understand how we can reduce waste at school.\n\nGood. We should explain that litter can harm a bird's habitat. I will ask the nature club to show a picture of one local species.\n\nYes, but first we will check the path with a teacher. The cleanup will start at three, after the hall discussion.\n\nOnly the bottles listed on the school notice. We should read the notice before we put anything in the box. Other garbage goes in the regular bin.\n\nYes. It is kept in the storage room, and the art group will turn it into new signs. That is one sustainable choice we can explain.\n\nBring it, please. We can put it beside the map of the lake and the ocean. The geography teacher is drawing arrows to show where the water goes.\n\nGreat. After the event, the ideas are read by the club, and we choose one to try the following month.",
